{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>Do not let your heads hang loose.</b> Since you are the ministers of HaKadosh Baruch Hu, it is not fitting for you to grieve and weep; but your brothers shall weep." "<b>And your garments you shall not tear.</b> Even though you are ordinary priests, today you are like a High Priest for the generations; and regarding the High Priest it is written: ״He shall not let his head hang loose and he shall not tear his garments,״ for this is the way of mourning, as it is written regarding the metzora: ״His garments shall be torn and his head shall be loose.״" "<b>And wrath will come upon all the congregation.</b> It refers back to above: ״you shall not die״ and ״upon all the congregation wrath shall not come״ — an analogy, as it is written: ״For not forever will He forget the needy; the hope of the poor shall not perish forever.״ Another interpretation: if you conduct mourning rites, HaKadosh Baruch Hu will be wrathful upon all the congregation. How so? He will not accept with favor the offerings that you have offered on behalf of the congregation."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:11:02.956120740Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}